# ── §8 honest C3 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

@? c3_arch_only_not_data :: step [d=2026-05-14 ok]
  => "all 5 directions assume v3-routing class corpus + d=512 toy substrate as data substrate. None test alternative corpus / probe / scale. Larger-scale data exploration (different anima-persona corpus, harder probes) is ORTHOGONAL paradigm shift not captured here"

@? c3_a2_trap_fundamental :: step [d=2026-05-14 ok]
  => "§A2-trap (z>3.0 robustness) may be FUNDAMENTAL to softmax routing under language modeling CE loss — escape may require leaving language modeling task entirely (e.g. fine-tune on classification head over category labels, then measure routing). This would require D3 design spec amendment"

@? c3_cost_uncertainty :: step [d=2026-05-14 ok]
  => "cost estimates are extrapolations from §52-§55 ($0.31/single fire). Architectural complexity (γ hierarchical, ε different class) may inflate train time / debug overhead by 2-5×. Real envelope could be $100-500 for full exploration"

@? c3_no_guarantee :: step [d=2026-05-14 ok]
  => "NONE of the 5 directions guarantee strict-4a achievement. They REPRESENT next-cycle hypotheses, NOT solved paths. Genuine architectural insight needed beyond enumeration — may require fundamental ML research input, not just dispatch"

@? c3_cond3_already_closed :: step [d=2026-05-14 ok]
  |> closure pragmatic note
  => "cond #3 ☑ MAINTAINED via §A3 4b composite — strict-4a polish is NOT closure-blocking. This .step ledger exists for completeness / future-cycle entry, not because cond #3 status is unstable"
